TITLE:: ViewKeycode
SUMMARY:: Platform scan codes for the keycode argument of LINK::Classes/View:: keyboard actions.
CATEGORIES:: GUI
RELATED:: Classes/ViewKeyModifier, Classes/ViewQtKey, Classes/ViewUnicode, Classes/SequencerKeyRouter

DESCRIPTION::
The fourth argument to LINK::Classes/View:: CODE::keyDownAction:: / CODE::keyUpAction:: is a platform-specific scan code. On Linux with Qt/X11, SuperCollider derives it from the X11 keycode (see QtCollider CODE::QWidgetProxy:: key handling).

Constants in this class are verified on Linux (X11). Values may differ on macOS or Windows; prefer CODE::char:: or CODE::ViewQtKey:: for portable bindings.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: backspace
Scan code for the Backspace key on Linux (X11).

METHOD:: control
Scan code for the Control key on Linux (X11).

METHOD:: downArrow
Scan code for the Down Arrow key on Linux (X11).

METHOD:: leftArrow
Scan code for the Left Arrow key on Linux (X11).

METHOD:: none
Zero; used when no meaningful scan code applies (for example Ctrl+letter chords matched only via CODE::ViewQtKey::).

METHOD:: rightArrow
Scan code for the Right Arrow key on Linux (X11).

METHOD:: tab
Scan code for the Tab key on Linux (X11).

METHOD:: upArrow
Scan code for the Up Arrow key on Linux (X11).
